            <ArticleTitle>Adverse effect of verapamil in myasthenia gravis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>396-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Verapamil, a class IV anti-arrhythmic drug that blocks voltage-dependent calcium channels in cardiac and smooth muscle, also has effects on presynaptic and postsynaptic voltage-dependent calcium channels at the neuromuscular junction. In a postoperative patient with pre-existent myasthenia gravis, oral verapamil caused a marked exacerbation in myasthenic weakness.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
